        "original_id": "50710344-c865-513e-9ee2-73faef1baaf4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Maskin, Leonid Hurwicz, Roger Myerson, Peter Sarnak, Abraham Flexner, Louis Bamberger, Caroline Bamberger Fuld\n- Organizations: Harvard University, Institute for Advanced Study\n- Places: Princeton, New Jersey, United States\n- Roles: Adams University Professor, permanent faculty\n- Concepts: mechanism design theory, Nobel Prize\n\nFacts:\n- Eric Maskin was born on December 12, 1950.\n- The Institute for Advanced Study was founded in 1930 by Abraham Flexner together with Louis Bamberger and Caroline Bamberger Fuld.\n- The Institute for Advanced Study is an independent postdoctoral research center for theoretical research and intellectual inquiry in Princeton, New Jersey, United States.\n- Eric Maskin is an American economist.\n- Eric Maskin won the 2007 Nobel Prize with Leonid Hurwicz and Roger Myerson for laying the foundations of mechanism design theory.\n- Eric Maskin is the Adams University Professor at Harvard University.\n- Peter Sarnak is on the permanent faculty at the School of Mathematics of the Institute for Advanced Study.",
